==== keepalived-advanced
h2: High Availability - Advanced VRRP
Advanced VRRP instance tuning. VIPs and instance assignment are in General.
h3: Global Settings
Keepalived global options and email notifications.
advanced.max_auto_priority [CBI.Value] Max Auto Priority: value=0 (placeholder "0")
  help: Set to 0 to disable auto-priority (recommended).
advanced.log_level [CBI.ListValue] HA Cluster Log Level: select=2 {0,1,2,3}
  help: Verbosity of ha-cluster shell scripts logging.
advanced.enable_notifications [CBI.FlagValue] Enable Email Notifications: [ ]
  help: Send email on state changes. Requires SMTP server.
h3: VRRP Instances
The General page creates a single "main" instance for atomic failover of all VIPs. Add extra instances here for independent failover groups.
| Name | VRID | Interface | VIPs | 
| main: main | 64 | lan | 1 | [☰][Edit][Delete]
<input> 
<button> Add
h3: Health Checks (VRRP Scripts)
Custom checks referenced by track_script. Examples: ping gateway, check DNS, verify VPN.
| Name | Script | 
| This section contains no values yet
<input> 
<button> Add
h3: State Change Hooks
Shell scripts executed on VRRP state changes. Click Edit to modify. Environment: $ACTION, $NAME, $TYPE.
| Name | 
| 01-ubus | [Edit]
| 01-user | [Edit]
<input> e.g., 60-vpn-failover
<button> Add
==== keepalived-advanced modal main
[tab General]
h4: High Availability - Advanced VRRP - main
main.vrid [CBI.Value] VRID: value=64
  help: Virtual Router ID (1-127). Must match on all cluster nodes. 128-255 reserved for auto-generated IPv6 instances.
main.interface [CBI.ListValue] Primary Interface: select=lan {backend,lan}
  help: Interface used for VRRP advertisements.
<button> Dismiss
<button> Save
[tab Timing]
h4: High Availability - Advanced VRRP - main
main.advert_int [CBI.Value] Advertisement Interval: value=1 (placeholder "1.0")
  help: VRRP advertisement frequency (seconds). Lower = faster failover. Default: 1.
main.priority [CBI.Value] Priority: value=100 (placeholder "Use global priority")
  help: Override global priority for this instance. Leave empty for global priority.
main.nopreempt [CBI.FlagValue] Keep Current MASTER (disable preemption): [x]
  help: Current MASTER stays MASTER even if higher-priority router returns.
main.preempt_delay [CBI.Value] Preempt Delay: value= (placeholder "30")
  help: Seconds before higher-priority router takes over. Prevents flapping. Recommended: 30-60.
main.garp_master_delay [CBI.Value] GARP Delay: value= (placeholder "5")
  help: Seconds before sending Gratuitous ARP after becoming MASTER. Helps with slow switches. Default: 5.
<button> Dismiss
<button> Save
[tab Authentication]
h4: High Availability - Advanced VRRP - main
main.auth_type [CBI.ListValue] Authentication Type: select=none {none,pass,ah}
  help: PASS: basic (max 8 chars, cleartext). AH: cryptographic (requires kmod-ipsec).
<button> Dismiss
<button> Save
[tab Tracking]
h4: High Availability - Advanced VRRP - main
main.track_interface [CBI.DynamicList] Track Interfaces: 
  help: Failover when tracked interface goes DOWN. Common: track WAN for internet failover.
main.track_script [CBI.DynamicList] Track Scripts: 
  help: Failover when health check fails. Define scripts in Health Checks section below.
<button> Dismiss
<button> Save
[tab Unicast]
h4: High Availability - Advanced VRRP - main
main.unicast_src_ip [CBI.Value] Unicast Source IP: value= (placeholder "e.g., 192.168.1.1")
  help: This router's address for unicast VRRP, in the family of a unicast peer. When empty, keepalived uses an address of the interface.
main.unicast_peer [CBI.DynamicList] Unicast Peer IPs: 
  help: Addresses of the other routers for unicast VRRP. Any entry makes this group unicast; only the peers in the family of the source IP, or else of the first peer, are used.
<button> Dismiss
<button> Save
==== owsync-advanced
h2: High Availability - Advanced Config Sync
Custom sync groups for services beyond General settings (e.g., VPN, mwan3).
h3: Global Settings
owsync global options.
advanced.sync_interval [CBI.Value] Poll Interval (seconds): value=30 (placeholder "30")
  help: Seconds between scans of the synced files. A local change is sent to the peers after the next scan.
advanced.owsync_log_level [CBI.ListValue] Log Level: select=2 {0,1,2,3}
  help: Verbosity of owsync daemon logging.
h3: Additional Sync Groups
Click Edit to configure files.
| Name | Status | Files | 
| This section contains no values yet
<input> 
<button> Add
h3: Exclusions
Files never synced; exclusions take precedence over sync groups. Default: network, system, owsync, ha-cluster, wireless.
<anon>.file [CBI.ChipListValue] Excluded Files: chip=network chip=system chip=owsync chip=ha-cluster chip=wireless value= (placeholder "/etc/dropbear/*.key") button "Add"
==== lease-sync-advanced
h2: High Availability - Advanced Lease Sync
Tuning for high-churn environments, unreliable networks, or troubleshooting.
h3: Lease-Sync Tuning
Default values work for most deployments.
advanced.lease_sync_port [CBI.Value] Sync Port: value=5378 (placeholder "5378")
  help: UDP port for lease sync.
advanced.lease_sync_interval [CBI.Value] Sync Interval: value=30 (placeholder "30")
  help: Seconds between full sync requests. Safety net for missed updates.
advanced.lease_sync_peer_timeout [CBI.Value] Peer Timeout: value=120 (placeholder "120")
  help: Seconds without heartbeat before peer is offline. Should be 4x sync_interval.
advanced.lease_sync_log_level [CBI.ListValue] Log Level: select=2 {0,1,2,3}
  help: Use Debug (3) for troubleshooting sync issues.
